---
description: 
globs: *.llm.mdx
alwaysApply: false
---
(mdx) A `llm.mdx` file contains markdown authored by a human.
(tsx) You should look for the corresponding `file.tsx` (tsx) file and compare the contents.
(page) The tsx file should be a Next.js app router `page.tsx` containing a translated version of the mdx file
(if-empty) If empty, you should convert the mdx to the tsx page
(if-absent) If there's no file, create one
(if-content) If there's content in the file, we must consider the context of the conversation and make the appropriate changes on both sides.
(use-markers) Use markers to ensure that it's easy to tell what part of the mdx is the tsx. Markers could be headings, or comments with slugs, or anything that an LLM can pick up on well.